   "spoken": "This is why more positional players prefer the knight to e2: with the knight on f3 you can't reroute to b3 because of a fork, and only the awkward queen to a4 holds d4 without the sac. The knight to e2 keeps everything defended and flexible.",
   "kind": "review",
   "teaches": "Ne2 defends d4 flexibly, avoiding the Ngf3 lines where Nb3 fails to a fork.",
   "plans": "Ne2 if you'd rather not sacrifice.",
