   "spoken": "Now the scary one: the pawn to g5. There was a time this was considered the outright refutation of the knight-f3 line. The idea is ...g4, throwing the knight off f3 and releasing White's grip on d4 — handled carelessly, the whole centre collapses.",
   "kind": "trap",
   "teaches": "...g5-g4 aims to evict the f3-knight and crash White's centre.",
