   "spoken": "When Black chases the queen with the bishop to g5, out comes the third trump — the pawn to f4. If Black takes en passant, the recapture on f3 leaves a decisive attack on f7; and if he defends, the retreating knight guards d4 in the most harmonious way. Black is already close to lost.",
   "kind": "trap",
   "teaches": "After ...Bg5, f4 is the breakthrough — the pressure on f7 becomes decisive.",
