   "spoken": "Here's the mind-expanding subtlety: after the knight to b4 and the bishop back to b1, castling kingside would be a serious mistake for Black. Commit the king to that side and, with the rook to e1, White's pressure condemns it to a lifetime of misery — the king is actually safer in the centre in this specific position.",
